[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":50},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":-7,"_26":27},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":48,"_13":48,"_37":49},"id","basico-cantos","nome","Corners in place","rascunho",false,"html","<p>The top face is yellow, but the corners may be swapped with each other. Now each corner goes to its place, by looking at the colors on the sides. This is the last step: at the end, the cube is solved.</p>\n<h2>Look for the headlights</h2>\n<p>Look at the sides of the top layer. When both corners on one side have the same color, like a car&#39;s two headlights, those two corners are right relative to each other.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R U R' U' R' F R2 U' R' U' R U R' F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/5ef007785a9f4558.svg\" alt=\"Red headlights on the left.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Red headlights on the left.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>The algorithm</h2>\n<p class=\"formula\"><code>R U R' U' R' F R2 U' R' U' R U R' F'</code></p>\n<p>It swaps the two corners on the right. It&#39;s the same one as in the 3x3 corners step. Break it into three parts to memorize: the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sexy-move\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The trigger R U R' U', the most common of all.\">sexy move</a> <code>R U R&#39; U&#39;</code>, then <code>R&#39; F R2 U&#39; R&#39;</code>, and finally <code>U&#39; R U R&#39; F&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>With headlights</strong>: turn the top (<code>U</code>) until the headlights are on the left. Do the algorithm.</p>\n<p><strong>No headlights</strong> (no side with two matching corners): do the algorithm from any side. Headlights appear, and you do it again with them on the left.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R U R' U' R' F R2 U' R' U' R U R' F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/c6210f817f90e79b.svg\" alt=\"Before: headlights on the left.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Before: headlights on the left.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/0db225cb4a4af944.svg\" alt=\"After the algorithm: the right corners swapped, and the cube solved.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>After the algorithm: the right corners swapped, and the cube solved.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;R U R' U' R' F R2 U' R' U' R U R' F' U&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/824b00f2cb5b9055.svg\" alt=\"Headlights at the back: `U'` brings them to the left, then the algorithm.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Headlights at the back: <code>U&#39;</code> brings them to the left, then the algorithm.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F R U' R' U' R U R' F' R U R' U' R' F R F'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/b488011afed4e838.svg\" alt=\"No headlights: the algorithm makes headlights appear; `U2` brings them to the left, the algorithm again, and `U` fixes the top.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>No headlights: the algorithm makes headlights appear; <code>U2</code> brings them to the left, the algorithm again, and <code>U</code> fixes the top.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>Fix the top</h2>\n<p>At the end, the 4 top corners are right relative to each other. Turn the top (<code>U</code>) until the side colors match the 1st layer.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;2x2&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;U&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/3c5473fd0ef58960.svg\" alt=\"Corners right relative to each other, but the top turned: `U'` fixes it.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Corners right relative to each other, but the top turned: <code>U&#39;</code> fixes it.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Done!</strong> The 2x2 is solved with two algorithms, the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sune\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Two short OLL algorithms that orient 3 corners: R U R' U R U2 R' (Sune) and R U2 R' U' R U' R' (Anti-Sune).\">Sune</a> and the headlights one, plus the sexy move for the 1st layer. Repeat until you don&#39;t need to look. When you want to go faster, the next step is <strong><a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a></strong>: the same 1st face, but without having to match the bottom sides.</p>\n</blockquote>\n","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=basico/cantos/casos","metodos",[43],"anterior",{"_13":41,"_37":42},"proximo","grupos",[28],{"_11":29,"_13":14,"_30":31,"_32":33,"_34":16,"_35":36,"_37":38},"2x2 Passo 3","nivel","iniciante","casos",2,"conjunto","ids",[39,40],"endereco","/2x2/basico/cantos/casos","2X2-B3-Dois-cantos-certos","2X2-B3-Nenhum-par-certo","Yellow face","/2x2/basico/face-amarela",{"_13":44,"_45":46,"_37":47},"Beginner method","numero",3,"/2x2/basico#cantos","2x2","/2x2/",{"_51":52,"_53":54},"cubos",[57,58,59,60,61,62,63],"idiomas",[55,56],"pt","en",{"_11":72,"_13":72},{"_11":48,"_13":48},{"_11":71,"_13":71},{"_11":70,"_13":70},{"_11":68,"_13":69},{"_11":66,"_13":67},{"_11":64,"_13":65},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
